  "description": "<div>\n<p>A keypad maps digits <code>2</code> through <code>9</code> to the letters printed on those keys: <code>2=abc, 3=def, 4=ghi, 5=jkl, 6=mno, 7=pqrs, 8=tuv, 9=wxyz</code>. Choose one letter for each digit in <code>digits</code> and return all resulting strings.</p>\n<p>Return the strings in alphabetical (lexicographic) order. An empty digit string has no combinations, so return <code>[]</code>. Repeated digits are independent choices.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> digits = &quot;23&quot;\n<strong>Output:</strong> [&quot;ad&quot;,&quot;ae&quot;,&quot;af&quot;,&quot;bd&quot;,&quot;be&quot;,&quot;bf&quot;,&quot;cd&quot;,&quot;ce&quot;,&quot;cf&quot;]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Each letter on 2 is paired with every letter on 3.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> digits = &quot;7&quot;\n<strong>Output:</strong> [&quot;p&quot;,&quot;q&quot;,&quot;r&quot;,&quot;s&quot;]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The 7 key offers four single-letter strings.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> digits = &quot;&quot;\n<strong>Output:</strong> []\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> No digits means there is nothing to choose a letter for.</pre>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>0 &lt;= digits.length &lt;= 4</code></li>\n<li><code>digits</code> contains only characters <code>2</code> through <code>9</code></li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
